event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1826,"item_id":"fc_05ead64b871aca2a016adb656cd45081918442bbb5ede3e67f","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped TensorProduct\\nnoncomputable def dividedPower (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] (f : V →ₗ[ℂ] V) (r : ℕ) : V →ₗ[ℂ] V := ((Nat.factorial r : ℂ)⁻¹) • (f ^ r)\\ndef LieIrreducible (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (x y h : E →ₗ[K] E) : Prop := Nontrivial E ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K E, (∀ z ∈ W, x z ∈ W) → (∀ z ∈ W, y z ∈ W) → (∀ z ∈ W, h z ∈ W) → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\\nnoncomputable def commAddEquiv {K : Type*} [Field K] (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] : M ⊗[ℤ] K ≃+ K ⊗[ℤ] M := by\\n  letI : Module ℤ (M ⊗[ℤ] K) := TensorProduct.instModule\\n  letI : Module ℤ (K ⊗[ℤ] M) := TensorProduct.instModule\\n  exact (TensorProduct.comm ℤ M K).toAddEquiv\\nnoncomputable instance sourceTensorModule {K : Type*} [Field K] (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] : Module K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) := AddEquiv.module K (@commAddEquiv K _ M _ _)\\nnoncomputable def sourceTensorAction {K : Type*} [Field K] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (f : M →ₗ[ℤ] M) : M ⊗[ℤ] K →ₗ[K] M ⊗[ℤ] K := by\\n  let e : M ⊗[ℤ] K ≃ₗ[K] K ⊗[ℤ] M := (@commAddEquiv K _ M _ _).linearEquiv K\\n  exact e.symm.toLinearMap.comp ((TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f).comp e.toLinearMap)\\nstructure LatticeInput (lam : ℤ) (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] where\\n  V : Type*\\n  [vAdd : AddCommGroup V]\\n  [vMod : Module ℂ V]\\n  basisV : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℂ V\\n  basisM : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℤ M\\n  embed : M →ₗ[ℤ] V\\n  x : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  y : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  h : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  xM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  yM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  hM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  v : V\\n  basis_compatible : ∀ i, basisV i = embed (basisM i)\\n  embed_injective : Function.Injective embed\\n  complex_irreducible : LieIrreducible ℂ V x y h\\n  x_compatible : ∀ m, embed (xM m) = x (embed m)\\n  y_compatible : ∀ m, embed (yM m) = y (embed m)\\n  h_compatible : ∀ m, embed (hM m) = h (embed m)\\n  divided_x_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V x r (embed m)\\n  divided_y_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V y r (embed m)\\ndef LatticeInput.H004 {lam : ℤ} {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (D : LatticeInput lam M) : Prop := by\\n  letI := D.vAdd\\n  letI := D.vMod\\n  exact (∀ w, D.h (D.x w) - D.x (D.h w) = (2:ℂ) • D.x w) ∧ (∀ w, D.h (D.y w) - D.y (D.h w) = (-2:ℂ) • D.y w) ∧ (∀ w, D.x (D.y w) - D.y (D.x w) = D.h w) ∧ D.v ≠ 0 ∧ D.x D.v = 0 ∧ D.h D.v = (lam:ℂ) • D.v ∧ (∀ i, D.basisV i = D.embed (D.basisM i)) ∧ Function.Injective D.embed ∧ LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.h ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.xM m) = D.x (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.yM m) = D.y (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.hM m) = D.h (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.x r (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.y r (D.embed m))\"},\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"K\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instK\",\"type\":\"Field K\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"p\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"instChar\",\"type\":\"CharP K p\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"hp\",\"type\":\"Nat.Prime p\"},{\"name\":\"lam\",\"type\":\"ℤ\"},{\"name\":\"hLam\",\"type\":\"(0:ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p:ℤ)\"},{\"name\":\"M\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instM\",\"type\":\"AddCommGroup M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instModM\",\"type\":\"Module ℤ M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"D\",\"type\":\"LatticeInput lam M\"},{\"name\":\"hD\",\"type\":\"LatticeInput.H004 D\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"Nat.Prime p\",\"H002\":\"CharP K p\",\"H003\":\"(0:ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p:ℤ)\",\"H004\":\"LatticeInput.H004 D\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (sourceTensorAction D.xM) (sourceTensorAction D.yM) (sourceTensorAction D.hM)\",\"representation\":\"M is an arbitrary free abelian lattice with a Z-basis whose embedded image is a C-basis of the complex irreducible highest-weight module V(lambda). Its operators are integral restrictions of the complex x,y,h operators and every divided power preserves it. The source-order carrier M tensor_Z K has a K-module structure transported by the additive tensor commutor from K tensor_Z M; the induced operators are conjugated from the standard lTensor action. H004 includes the source-stated characteristic-zero irreducibility, highest-vector relations, Lie brackets and lattice conditions. The representation retains arbitrary M, p=2 and lambda=0, with no assumption that reduced h-weights remain distinct. The commutor transport is an actual definition, not a conversion comment.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (sourceTensorAction D.xM) (sourceTensorAction D.yM) (sourceTensorAction D.hM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\",\"S002\",\"S003\",\"S004\",\"S005\",\"S006\",\"S007\",\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"One substantive closed obligation covering the complete accepted route. Later proof work must establish the divided-power basis and endpoint formulas in characteristic zero; calculate matrix-unit composites and invert their binomial coefficients in Z_(p), including p=2 and lambda=0; analyze coordinate modules for the arbitrary localized lattice, compute fraction-field dimension before proving the rank-one generator by the valuation argument; reduce the resulting lattice basis and x,y,h action matrices to the source tensor construction; then apply reduced matrix units to a chosen nonzero vector in any nonzero invariant subspace and discharge the zero/nonzero cases. Witnesses remain local to the nonzero branch. This is the exact source output obligation rather than a True surrogate.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T001\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T001\"}}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":1827,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_05ead64b871aca2a016adb656cd45081918442bbb5ede3e67f","call_id":"call_35f89be1002148bd938b34fd7159fe03","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped TensorProduct\\nnoncomputable def dividedPower (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] (f : V →ₗ[ℂ] V) (r : ℕ) : V →ₗ[ℂ] V := ((Nat.factorial r : ℂ)⁻¹) • (f ^ r)\\ndef LieIrreducible (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (x y h : E →ₗ[K] E) : Prop := Nontrivial E ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K E, (∀ z ∈ W, x z ∈ W) → (∀ z ∈ W, y z ∈ W) → (∀ z ∈ W, h z ∈ W) → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\\nnoncomputable def commAddEquiv {K : Type*} [Field K] (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] : M ⊗[ℤ] K ≃+ K ⊗[ℤ] M := by\\n  letI : Module ℤ (M ⊗[ℤ] K) := TensorProduct.instModule\\n  letI : Module ℤ (K ⊗[ℤ] M) := TensorProduct.instModule\\n  exact (TensorProduct.comm ℤ M K).toAddEquiv\\nnoncomputable instance sourceTensorModule {K : Type*} [Field K] (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] : Module K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) := AddEquiv.module K (@commAddEquiv K _ M _ _)\\nnoncomputable def sourceTensorAction {K : Type*} [Field K] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (f : M →ₗ[ℤ] M) : M ⊗[ℤ] K →ₗ[K] M ⊗[ℤ] K := by\\n  let e : M ⊗[ℤ] K ≃ₗ[K] K ⊗[ℤ] M := (@commAddEquiv K _ M _ _).linearEquiv K\\n  exact e.symm.toLinearMap.comp ((TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f).comp e.toLinearMap)\\nstructure LatticeInput (lam : ℤ) (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] where\\n  V : Type*\\n  [vAdd : AddCommGroup V]\\n  [vMod : Module ℂ V]\\n  basisV : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℂ V\\n  basisM : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℤ M\\n  embed : M →ₗ[ℤ] V\\n  x : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  y : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  h : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  xM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  yM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  hM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  v : V\\n  basis_compatible : ∀ i, basisV i = embed (basisM i)\\n  embed_injective : Function.Injective embed\\n  complex_irreducible : LieIrreducible ℂ V x y h\\n  x_compatible : ∀ m, embed (xM m) = x (embed m)\\n  y_compatible : ∀ m, embed (yM m) = y (embed m)\\n  h_compatible : ∀ m, embed (hM m) = h (embed m)\\n  divided_x_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V x r (embed m)\\n  divided_y_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V y r (embed m)\\ndef LatticeInput.H004 {lam : ℤ} {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (D : LatticeInput lam M) : Prop := by\\n  letI := D.vAdd\\n  letI := D.vMod\\n  exact (∀ w, D.h (D.x w) - D.x (D.h w) = (2:ℂ) • D.x w) ∧ (∀ w, D.h (D.y w) - D.y (D.h w) = (-2:ℂ) • D.y w) ∧ (∀ w, D.x (D.y w) - D.y (D.x w) = D.h w) ∧ D.v ≠ 0 ∧ D.x D.v = 0 ∧ D.h D.v = (lam:ℂ) • D.v ∧ (∀ i, D.basisV i = D.embed (D.basisM i)) ∧ Function.Injective D.embed ∧ LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.h ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.xM m) = D.x (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.yM m) = D.y (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.hM m) = D.h (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.x r (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.y r (D.embed m))\"},\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"K\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instK\",\"type\":\"Field K\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"p\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"instChar\",\"type\":\"CharP K p\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"hp\",\"type\":\"Nat.Prime p\"},{\"name\":\"lam\",\"type\":\"ℤ\"},{\"name\":\"hLam\",\"type\":\"(0:ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p:ℤ)\"},{\"name\":\"M\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instM\",\"type\":\"AddCommGroup M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instModM\",\"type\":\"Module ℤ M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"D\",\"type\":\"LatticeInput lam M\"},{\"name\":\"hD\",\"type\":\"LatticeInput.H004 D\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"Nat.Prime p\",\"H002\":\"CharP K p\",\"H003\":\"(0:ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p:ℤ)\",\"H004\":\"LatticeInput.H004 D\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (sourceTensorAction D.xM) (sourceTensorAction D.yM) (sourceTensorAction D.hM)\",\"representation\":\"M is an arbitrary free abelian lattice with a Z-basis whose embedded image is a C-basis of the complex irreducible highest-weight module V(lambda). Its operators are integral restrictions of the complex x,y,h operators and every divided power preserves it. The source-order carrier M tensor_Z K has a K-module structure transported by the additive tensor commutor from K tensor_Z M; the induced operators are conjugated from the standard lTensor action. H004 includes the source-stated characteristic-zero irreducibility, highest-vector relations, Lie brackets and lattice conditions. The representation retains arbitrary M, p=2 and lambda=0, with no assumption that reduced h-weights remain distinct. The commutor transport is an actual definition, not a conversion comment.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (sourceTensorAction D.xM) (sourceTensorAction D.yM) (sourceTensorAction D.hM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\",\"S002\",\"S003\",\"S004\",\"S005\",\"S006\",\"S007\",\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"One substantive closed obligation covering the complete accepted route. Later proof work must establish the divided-power basis and endpoint formulas in characteristic zero; calculate matrix-unit composites and invert their binomial coefficients in Z_(p), including p=2 and lambda=0; analyze coordinate modules for the arbitrary localized lattice, compute fraction-field dimension before proving the rank-one generator by the valuation argument; reduce the resulting lattice basis and x,y,h action matrices to the source tensor construction; then apply reduced matrix units to a chosen nonzero vector in any nonzero invariant subspace and discharge the zero/nonzero cases. Witnesses remain local to the nonzero branch. This is the exact source output obligation rather than a True surrogate.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T001\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T001\"}}","status":"completed"}}

